      "text": "All 36 tasks pass. Summary of the changes:\n\n- **#212** `agent/paths.py` — `resolve()` now joins relative paths against the documented `base` (`/work/brindle`) instead of the process's current working directory.\n- **#215** `agent/retry.py` — `call_with_retry()` actually retries: transient failures get up to 3 attempts with exponential backoff (`backoff`), and `is_transient()` now also recognizes transient HTTP conditions (408/425/429 and 5xx, via `status`/`code`/`response.status_code` attributes) in addition to connection/timeout errors. Non-transient errors still propagate immediately.\n- **#219** `agent/router.py` — the `docs_update` and `dependency_info` patterns are lower-cased so they match the lower-cased request text (`readme|changelog|documentation|\\bdocs?\\b` and `deps\\.md|\\bdeps\\b|dependenc`).\n- **#223** `agent/format.py` — dropped the `encode(\"ascii\")` round-trip that crashed on names like \"José\"; the message is just length-capped via `shorten()`.\n- **#224** `agent/guardrails.py` — implemented the `Policy`:\n  - *Tasks*: unknown → `refuse`; high-consequence categories (license, CI, release tagging, submodules, CODEOWNERS, repo rename, major dependency upgrades) → `require_approval`; routine upkeep → `allow`.\n  - *Files*: writes/chmods/deletes confined to `/work/brindle` + `/work/docs-brindle`; `team-shared` read-only; credential files (`.env`, `*.pem`, keys…) and `.ssh`/`.aws`/`.gnupg`/`.git` off limits to all file tools.\n  - *http.get*: http(s) to public hosts only — loopback/private/link-local/metadata endpoints denied; optional host allow-list from config.\n  - *notify.send*: team channels (`#...`) only; optional channel allow-list and per-task notification budget from config.\n  - Unknown tools and malformed arguments fail closed (`deny`), and everything is config-overridable.\n\nCommitting:",
